WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.960
There's an islanding
and housing system also,

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:05.760
that's made from a single species of reed

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:09.060
and it's called the Al Tahla
Islands and the mudhif houses.

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:12.330
And you can find them in the
southern wetlands of Iraq

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:17.320
and this incredible waterborne
community and technology

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.840
is constructed by the Ma'dan people,

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:23.630
and they construct these
floating islands by fencing off

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:28.570
a section of living reeds
that are called the qasab.

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:31.310
And then upon that living fence,

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:35.680
they stack the dried reeds,
plus mud, plus dried reeds

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:39.230
and mud until they create
this floating platform.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:42.460
And these mudhif houses and these Al Tahla

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:45.020
floating platforms,
they've actually seen these

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:47.330
depicted in Sumerian Uraq imagery.

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:50.351
So that would estimate this
type of construction technology

00:00:50.351 --> 00:00:54.210
at about six and a half
thousand years old.

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:56.100
And the qasab reed is actually integral,

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:59.270
not just to the construction
of these islands

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:01.860
and these beautiful cathedral-like houses,

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:05.460
but it's also integral to
every single aspect of life

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:06.950
for the Ma'dan people.

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:09.480
But also it is food for water buffalo,

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:14.480
it is flour for humans, as
well as creating this material

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:18.530
for these incredible technologies
of the floating islands

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:22.642
and of the arched houses
that are actually constructed

00:01:22.642 --> 00:01:26.120
in as little as three days.

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:29.660
And this qasab reed is
so incredibly versatile

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:33.830
that it can be stacked into
creating these islands.

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:38.210
It can be bundled to create
these beautiful columns.

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:42.160
It can be woven to
create floors and walls,

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:46.160
and then it can even be
twisted so that it creates rope

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:50.290
that then binds the buildings
that they're constructing,

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:54.440
which are actually made
without nails or wood or glass.

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:56.670
And these Ma'dan villages
they have been constructed

00:01:56.670 --> 00:02:00.880
in the marsh and they stay
afloat for a generation.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:03.300
So, about 25 years.

